I again left a broken leftover line in runOcr's pdf branch (`const jpgBlob=...` nonsense that draws editorPageCanvas — totally wrong). The problem: runOcrPage discards the canvas after recognition, but for searchable PDF I need the rendered page image. Restructure: runOcrPage should return the JPEG blob directly instead of dims only.

Clean design:
```js
async function runOcrPage(pdf,i,lang,wantHocr){
  render canvas
  const Tesseract=await loadTesseract()
  const {data}=await Tesseract.recognize(canvas,lang,{...},{text:true,hocr:wantHocr})
  const result={text:data.text||'',hocr:data.hocr||'',width:canvas.width,height:canvas.height,size:base}
  if(wantHocr){result.jpg=await new Promise(r=>canvas.toBlob(r,'image/jpeg',.8))}
  canvas.width=1;canvas.height=1
  return result
}
```
Then in runOcr pdf branch: embedJpg(await r.jpg.arrayBuffer()), drawImage full page, then words overlay.

