Also note space tokens between words: tokens include whitespace tokens; when wrapping, a space at line end adds width; drop trailing spaces when pushing line (handled). Space token mid-line contributes width — good. Also drawText of a space token — fine (empty draw) but we can skip drawing pure-space tokens in drawLine (they only contribute width): in the drawing loop, skip if !t.word.trim().

