    - Else insert table AFTER the caret's block (or before if caret at very start of block? Keep simple: insert after the block).
  - Else append at end of last page.
- Then remove the now-empty paragraph if we inserted before an empty one? If we insert before an empty <p>, leave it (it acts as trailing paragraph). Actually then you'd have table + empty p + rest — fine (the trailing <p><br></p> I append after the table would duplicate empties). Adjust: if inserted before an EMPTY paragraph, don't add the extra `<p><br></p>`.
- Add a real focused check? No focus needed with DOM insertion.
- Also scrollIntoView + focus the first cell? Better UX: place caret in first cell so user can start typing: `td.focus()`.

