1: # @mssio/qpdf-wasm
2: 
3: [qpdf](https://github.com/qpdf/qpdf), the PDF transformation tool, compiled to WebAssembly.
4: Merge, split, rotate, encrypt, decrypt, linearize and compress PDFs **in the browser or Node**,
5: with no server and no native dependencies.
6: 
7: [![npm](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/@mssio/qpdf-wasm)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@mssio/qpdf-wasm)
8: [![CI](https://github.com/mssio/qpdf-wasm/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/mssio/qpdf-wasm/actions/workflows/ci.yml)
9: [![license](https://img.shields.io/npm/l/@mssio/qpdf-wasm)](./LICENSE)
10: 
11: <!-- qpdf-version -->Contains qpdf 12.4.2, built unmodified for WebAssembly.<!-- /qpdf-version -->
12: At runtime: `import { qpdfVersion } from "@mssio/qpdf-wasm"`.
13: 
14: > This is an independent project, not an official qpdf release. qpdf is built **unmodified** from its
15: > upstream source.
16: 
17: ## Why
18: 
19: - **The real qpdf**: every qpdf feature is reachable, including through the raw CLI (`run()`).
20: - **Runs in a Web Worker** by default, so your UI never freezes.
21: - **Works with any framework**: plain ESM + Promises + TypeScript types. React, Vue, Svelte, Angular, vanilla.
22: - **Zero bundler config** with Vite and webpack 5 (tested); see Bundlers & hosting for others.
23: - **Lazy**: the ~700 KB (gzip) wasm downloads only when you call `createQpdf()`.
24: 
25: ## Install
26: 
27: ```sh
28: npm install @mssio/qpdf-wasm
29: ```
30: 
31: TypeScript users need TypeScript ≥ 5.7: outputs are typed `Uint8Array<ArrayBuffer>`, so `new Blob([output])`
32: type-checks.
33: 
34: ## Quick start
35: 
36: ```js
37: import { createQpdf } from "@mssio/qpdf-wasm";
38: 
39: const qpdf = await createQpdf();                 // starts a worker, loads qpdf.wasm
40: const [a, b] = document.querySelector("input[type=file]").files;
41: const { output } = await qpdf.merge([a, b]);     // File/Blob, Uint8Array or ArrayBuffer
42: const url = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([output], { type: "application/pdf" }));
43: window.open(url);
44: ```
45: 
